# Pre-mortem — V2i onboarding seed (revised after v1 falsification)
- date: 2026-09-27
- branch: fix/cli-254-v2i-theme-picker-seed
- lenses: [gary-klein, saltzer-schroeder, michael-feathers]

## v1 result
Falsified. CI run 36333931759, exit 31. Seed at ~/.claude/settings.json
did not skip picker. Root cause: wrong file path. Claude reads
onboarding state from ~/.claude.json, not ~/.claude/settings.json.

## v2 risks

### R1 — Klein (change impact)
Seed lands in Docker image only. Adopter machines unaffected.
Cost if wrong: rebuild image; drop the COPY line; revert.

### R2 — Klein (unmet prerequisite)
v2 assumes ~/.claude.json is the current v2.1.x path. If Anthropic
changes it in a future release, seed goes stale silently.
- Falsification: drive.log after v2 run. If picker still fires, path
  changed OR another gate exists.
- Cure: extend seed for the next gate; or add /adopter/.config/claude/
  alt path.

### R3 — Feathers (silent regression)
Seed could mask a new gate added in a future Claude release. Drive.log
stays authoritative.

### R4 — Saltzer-Schroeder (least privilege)
Seed lands with adopter:adopter ownership per COPY --chown. No other
user in container reads or writes it.

### R5 — Klein (working-directory drift)
Seed hardcodes /home/adopter/test as the trusted project. If bassclef
init ever runs in a different cwd, the trust dialog fires. Current
smoke output confirms /home/adopter/test is the cwd.
- Mitigation: if init cwd changes, update the projects key.

### R6 — Klein (image-size drift)
Seed adds ~150 bytes + one COPY layer. Negligible.

## Strongest concerns folded in
- R2 — path may change. Falsification via drive.log after v2 run.
- R5 — cwd hardcoded. Assert-verified via smoke output.

## Verdict
Ship v2. Risks bounded and observable via drive.log.
